+#### Mixpanel
+
+Mixpanel supports two authentication methods. Select one using the **Authentication** toggle when setting up a Mixpanel import.
+
+- **Service account** – Requires a service account username, secret, and your Mixpanel project ID. Create a service account under **Organization settings** > **Service accounts** in Mixpanel and give it access to the project you're importing. Find your project ID under **Project settings** > **Project Details**. See [Mixpanel's service account docs](https://docs.mixpanel.com/reference/service-accounts).
+
+- **Project secret** – Requires the project secret only. Find it under **Project settings** > **Access keys** in Mixpanel. See [Mixpanel's docs](https://docs.mixpanel.com/docs/orgs-and-projects/managing-projects#access-keys). Newer Mixpanel projects may not have a project secret – use a service account instead.
+
+#### Amplitude
+
+Amplitude requires an API key and secret key. Both are needed for Amplitude's Export API, which uses Basic auth.
 
